Subject: [PATCH] gl: serve every GL limit the measured GPU reports

getParameter returns the measured GPU's value for every limit it
records, including zero and negative values such as
MAX_SERVER_WAIT_TIMEOUT and MIN_PROGRAM_TEXEL_OFFSET, fractional ranges
such as ALIASED_POINT_SIZE_RANGE, and MAX_VIEWPORT_DIMS. The hooks cover
the robust getters the passthrough decoder calls, so limits Blink
queries live match the ones it caches. ANGLE on Mesa llvmpipe counts as
a backend that enforces nothing, like SwiftShader. A Direct3D 11
renderer string beside a 16384 viewport or the host's point size range
is a contradiction a page finds with one call.

